    "text": ", and we specialize in the essential accessibility retrofits that secure your home. We can install heavy-duty grab bars, change out your round door knobs for comfortable lever \n\nhandles, secure your stair handrails, mount task lighting, and make minor threshold adjustments. Anything that calls for a licensed residential builder or a licensed trade is coordinated with a licensed pro. Our services are perfectly tailored to these high-impact safety modifications!\nLooking to execute any of these changes?\nAAA Handyman Services LLC can help you plan, measure, and install many of the minor accessibility modifications listed below (such as grab bars, handrails, lever handles, or simple ramps) to secure your home's future comfort.\nJump to section:\nExterior\nFloor Plan\nDoors & Windows\nGarage & Carport\nKitchen & Appliances\nBathroom\nStairways & Elevators\nStorage & Controls\nHVAC & Flooring\nConvenience & Misc\nLive Home Walkthrough Tracker\n0 of 28 items checked\n0%\nReset Progress\nGet Printable Assessment Kit\nAAA Handyman Services LLC\nAging-in-Place Walk-Through Assessment Kit\nOakland County, Michigan · (248) 385-3432 · contact@aaahandyman.services\nSafety · Access · Comfort\nHomeowner / resident:\nAssessment date:\nProperty address:\nCompleted by:\nExterior Considerations\nLow-maintenance exterior (vinyl, brick) and low-maintenance shrubs and plants\nTedious tasks of today will become more difficult ones down the road. Without family members to assist, it may be wiser to purchase lower-effort greenery and exterior surfaces.\nDeck, patio, or balcony surfaces\nMake sure these surfaces are no more than a half inch below interior floor level if they’re made of wood.\nOverall Floor Plan Considerations\nMain living on a single story\nThis includes having a full bath on the main level. Older residents will have a simpler time without having to climb additional stairs for basic necessities.\nReducing Steps\nBuilds should limit the amount of stairs being built, especially to even out"
